<section class="problem">
  <div class="problem-inner">
    <p class="label">The problem</p>
    <h2 class="problem-headline">Most factories are flying blind<br>on their own waste streams.</h2>
    <p class="problem-statement">Plant managers handle waste every day without knowing its actual value. Manual sorting is slow, market prices shift hourly, and ESG compliance is still done by hand. By the time the waste leaves the facility, most of its value is already gone.</p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-number">01</div>
        <h3>Hidden value</h3>
        <p>Factories discard materials worth real money — because information doesn't exist at the point of disposal. What looks like trash is often copper, aluminum, or rare earths.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-number">02</div>
        <h3>Outdated tracking</h3>
        <p>Spreadsheets and manual reports can't keep pace with hourly market fluctuations in secondary materials. Most plants are 3–6 months behind on pricing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <div class="problem-number">03</div>
        <h3>Compliance burden</h3>
        <p>ESG reporting requirements are multiplying. Calculating avoided CO₂ by hand is time-consuming and error-prone — and increasingly required by law.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
